course: dictionary
lesson: 12106
title: Coinage: money, making coins, and new words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Coinage has three meanings. It can mean the coins a country uses and its money system, such as decimal coinage with 100 pence in a pound. It can mean the act of making coins. It can also mean a new word or phrase that someone has invented.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. «The old coinage had twelve pennies in a shilling, so the sums were hard.» The words money and sums show that coinage means the coins and the money system.
explain: «The word selfie is a modern coinage.» Here there are no coins at all. The word modern and the word word show that coinage means a new word that someone has invented.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. If «new word» fits the sentence and still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Careful: to coin a phrase means to invent a saying.
fact: Coinage means the coins a country uses, and its whole system of money.
fact: «Decimal coinage» means money counted in tens and hundreds, with 100 pence in a pound.
fact: Coinage can also mean making coins, or inventing a new word or phrase.
fact: «Selfie» is a modern coinage: someone invented it, and now it is in the dictionary.
fact: To «coin a phrase» means to invent a saying.
exercise: «The museum showed coins from the coinage of ancient Rome.» What does coinage mean here? | A kind of cake baked for festivals | *The coins a country uses and its money system | A long walk in the hills
exercise: What does «coined» mean in this sentence? «Maya coined a new word, snackarooni, and the whole class started using it.» | *Invented | Counted | Lost | Painted
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that names money: «The class learned about decimal coinage in maths.» | learned | class | *coinage | maths
test: «The mint was busy all day with coinage, turning out shiny new coins.» What does coinage mean in this sentence? | A type of shoe | A quiet, gloomy mood | A school holiday | *Making coins
test: Dad says, «I'll coin a phrase: a hungry dog never waits.» What does coin a phrase mean? | Pay for a meal with coins | Speak very slowly | Count the coins in a jar | *Invent a saying
exam: «Nobody had used the word before, so the teacher said it was a brand new coinage.» What does coinage mean? | The price of a snack | *A new word that someone has invented | A kind of wallet | Coins that are no longer used
